(entity report 5167-1): The first entity reported in relation to SCP-5167. SCP-5167-3-1 is a quadruped creature mildly resembling a reptilian canine from dimension 1. Average height is at approximately 1.5 meters from the shoulders and 3.7 meters in length. They also possess large quills along the spine and a prehensile tail.

First reported in 1947 and by 1949 were eradicated from the region. While 13 of the creatures were captured, none survived in captivity by 6 months.

(entity report 5167-2): In 1959 a previously unknown species of earthworm, named Lumbricus Badensis, was discovered in the black forest region of Germany. Through foundation research it was discovered that the worm had originated from dimension [██] within site [REDACTED].

It is believed that they burrowed beneath the dirt and had made their way beyond the containment zone into the wild. It was at this point that the underground barrier was constructed to prevent any similar incidents. Initially believed benign, records were changed and amnestics were distributed to make it appear that they were always native to the region as well as other measures taken to assure containment within the region. However, there were soon reports of 7 meters long worms within the black forest. It was discovered that for current reasons unknown some of the worms do not stop growing beyond a certain point and will continue to grow indefinitely while consuming vast amounts of local flora. Greater measures have been taken to curb and possibly eliminate the population and to hunt down excessively large instances.




