Since the foundation established site [REDACTED], there have been [██] dimensional shifts created by SCP-5167-2. MTF Phi-9 (“World Jumpers”) was created to explore the dimensions accessed by SCP-5167-2 for both recon and scientific study purposes. The following is a list of those shifts.

Dimension 1: The first dimension recorded by the foundation was on the day the location was discovered on 03/11/1947 by an MTF unit. It only lasted until 14/11/1947 and as such the foundation was unfortunately unable to send an MTF unit in for exploration purposes. Multiple SCP-5167-3-1 were reported exiting from the dimension before it shifted confirming their point of origin.

Visual observation showed a rocky and desolate terrain with little flora and almost no other fauna. Several other smaller entities were captured though none survived captivity as the biological and atmospheric differences between the creatures and dimension were most likely vastly different.

Dimension 2: On 14/11/1947 at 16:11 hours, SCP-5167-2 sounded an alarm and placed the base on lockdown as the reality within the exclusion zone began to destabilize. For 5 minutes and 11 seconds a form of event horizon formed within the zone. Immediately after the event dissipated another dimension had replaced the previous one. An MTF unit, Phi-9 (“World Jumpers”), was soon formed to carry out the expedition and recon missions in the dimension and any other subsequent dimensions.

Visual observation showed a volcanic terrain with many lava flows and high temperatures. The unit was outfitted with pressurized environmental suits to survive the high sulfur level and two-way radio sets to be used at intervals when the gate function is activated. The rest of the region beyond the perimeter similarly matched the exclusion zone. Large volcanos and rivers of molten lava make up most of the dimension. Areas not covered by lava are large ash pits and plains of obsidian and other igneous rocks.

While on an expedition into the region, MTF Phi-9 encountered what appeared to be inhabitants of the dimension. Descriptions and photographs of the beings show them to be humanoids roughly 5 meters in height with very coarse and thick skin that matched and camouflaged them in their environment making them hard to detect despite their large size. While never aggressive they actively avoided all MTF members though could occasionally be spotted trailing and watching the units. Despite wide reconnaissance of the region, no habitations or structures possibly belonging to the creatures were ever found or even small groups of them.

Dimension 3: On 23/03/1955 at 02:56 hours, the dimension once again shifted. The dimension resembled the nearby black forest and was inhabited by a wide variety of both flora and fauna, the latter of which were included many hostile creatures. The most dangerous of these were a large Canid creature resembling the species Canis Lupus. Defensive barriers had to be placed around the already existing energy wall as the creatures were highly agile and able to clear the fence to attack personnel on the base. As well as agility the creatures were also highly resistant to both pain and damage, able to easily withstand small arms fire. Anti-tank and heavy weapons had the most effect on killing them when they appeared to attack the barrier. Due to the hostile nature of the local wildlife, no recon missions were carried out in the region due to the danger and high probability of casualties on missions.

Dimension 4: The next shift was on 17/08/1958 at 12:33 hours. The Dimension resembled a swamp environment with many bogs and rivers intersecting the landscape. Hydrogen sulfide and methane was very common in the local atmosphere as well as other chemicals that had a corroding effect on the nearby barrier fence and foundation equipment. This combined with the massive snakes like creatures that inhabited this dimension made exploration on foot quite difficult with most recon being carried out by newly acquired airborne assets. The largest of the instances was estimated to be within 16 to 18 meters long though since most of its body was underwater it’s possible it was much larger.

It was from this dimension that SCP-5167-3-2 originated and entered ours. Since the creature’s arrival into the local ecosystem, vast amounts of flora have been destroyed by larger specimens of the species as well as higher concentration of both methane and hydrogen sulfide. It was at this time that the underground barrier was constructed to prevent a breach of containment on this level from happening again.

Dimension 5: The first site wide incident occurred on 11/06/1962 when the zone changed dimension at 07:48 hours. A red alert message was received from Site [REDACTED] by a nearby Foundation run installation. The message detailed that all personnel on the base had been killed by an unknown agent leaving only those in the airlocked command center alive after SCP-XXX-2 had once again switched dimensions. It was soon determined by a foundation hazmat/biological contamination crew that a highly toxic substance (later determined to be an inorganic molecule composed of Arsenic, Sulfur and a previously unknown element) originating from the new dimension. Fortunately, the toxin did not ever travel beyond the outer perimeter of the site and all remaining personnel were successfully evacuated. Atmospheric sensors were set up at this time to determine where personnel could survive without a hazmat suit (all areas 1.7 kilometers of the barrier except the protected command center were deemed hostile to all life).

Observation of the dimension showed a landscape covered and possibly entirely composed of crystalline structures resembling a forest. This includes not just all flora but fauna as well with all known instances being made of crystalline material. Elements not traditionally associated with crystal formation are also somehow incorporated as well as never before encountered elements and compounds such as the toxin that compromised the base.

Dimension 6: The next shift occurred on 05/08/1964 at 03:27 hours. After the all clear alarm had sounded post conclusion of atmospheric tests, observation of the dimension showed an alpine forest and tundra covered in snow. A wide variety of both flora and fauna similar to our own existed in the region as well as inhabitant humanoid beings similar to those discovered in Dimension 2. While many of the reported inhabitants more closely resembled humans, many were also far more varied in appearance with some barely resembling humans. Temperament also greatly varied between them with some being apathetic to our appearance while others were openly hostile. Communication between the foundation and the humanoids has been very limited due to both their language being completely unknown to us and their linguistic processes widely different than our own. Aerial reconnaissance showed a massive citadel city approximately 47 kilometers from the reality wall.




