Interviewee:  Dr. [REDACTED] Braun

Interviewer:  Agent [REDACTED]

Notes: Dr. Braun was one the few confirmed Obskurakorps scientist to be listed in the few remaining files found at the site when the foundation first discovered it. He had been a high priority POI for his role at the site and his likely knowledge of many unknowns pertaining to this particular SCP as well as other SCP's pertaining to the GOI. He was apprehended 17 hours prior to this interview in Switzerland living under a new identity while still retaining connections to the GOI.



[BEGIN LOG] 

(extraneous dialogue excluded)

(translated from German)

Agent : Now onto your position at the SCP-5167 site. We wish for you to explain to the best of your ability the creation of the machine at the site and what purpose it served as well as all knowledge pertaining to project Ragnarök.

Dr Braun : You might as well be asking me how to explain the nature of the entire universe.

Agent : We know you were positioned at the site as a head researcher. There is no denying your detailed knowledge of the site and project.

Dr Braun : I am not denying my position there, however, it is not as simple to explain the project as you may think, especially since I'm not much more educated on the subject than you. I’m sure you’re aware with working for the Foundation of need to know protocols concerning information. I was told only what was necessary to complete my part of the project.

Agent : Any information you have will still be needed despite that. Now explain your role and any information you had on the project.

Dr Braun : The project put very simply was to ensure the survival of the aryan race above all others despite any outcome in the war. As well as to accomplish any other goals Dr. Schuster may have in mind.

Agent : Who is Dr. Schuster?

Dr Braun : The main director and leader of the project. He was placed in charge of the project by Weiss and Himmler due to his knowledge of Norse mythology and thaumatology as well as his own push for the creation of the project. I was then chosen by him to oversee the site and to carry out experiments with the entity. Where it came from and how it was made is completely unknown to me. I was only responsible to carry out required experiments with it and complete any projects he gave me while he supervised them as well as experiments at other sites connected to the project.

Agent : What do you know of these other sites?

Dr Braun : I did not learn much of the other sites as they did not pertain to my research, only that the entity was created or found at one of these sites. As far as I know ours was the main site of the project with mostly historical and archeological research being carried out by the others.

Agent : So, do you know at the very least how to fully operate it?

Dr Braun : As you are most likely aware of at this point it functions autonomously of human operation with only minimal human oversight. The calculations it runs continuously are far beyond anything a human can comprehend or ever hope to accomplish in a lifetime. What I do know is that it finds other dimensions and opens them to us. It also appears to not be searching just for any ones that are available, but for particular ones. I don’t know what he ever found to bring him to this conclusion, but I do know that Dr. Schuster found something that led him to believe that the nine realms of Norse mythology and the stories surrounding them were in fact real or at least based on some fact. He believed if we could travel to these places, we could unlock their mysteries and find ways to ensure Germany’s thousand years Reich and possibly beyond into the new world.

Agent : What new world?

Dr Braun : Do you know nothing of Norse history? Do you not know what Ragnarök is?

Agent : I am aware of some Norse mythology and of how Ragnarök was their story of the apocalypse. I need specifics though, no guessing, just straight answers.

Dr Braun : Ragnarök was more than just an apocalypse, it was a rebirth of the world. According to them the world began in chaos and will end in chaos but from it two humans will survive and begin anew. One of the goals he wanted to achieve was that if any humans were to survive any end of the current world, it would be us and no other. Besides that possibility it was also possible we would find something with which to win the war. Of course, as you know that did not happen.

Agent : So, the project was a failure then?

Dr Braun : No. The project did not fail. I told you already that it was to ensure Germany’s survival despite any outcome to the war. When it was becoming clear that Germany would soon fall with the red army pushing in from the east and the allies from the west, new objectives were given. Research, artifacts, personnel and supplies were moved into the most recently opened dimension. It was one that he himself personally directed the machine to open to though I have no idea how. It was there that a new base was established, one the allies could not get to, so that even when Germany fell, he could continue the project. Only he and his select personnel of Obskurakorps members crossed over and when word reached us that the allies were quickly approaching, the machine cut off access and for the first time ever initiated shutdown. I and everyone else left at the site soon evacuated. To be honest I am not quite sure how the machine managed to restart once again or why it did so.

Agent : Are you saying he and many others are still out there? Do you have any information on the dimension?

Dr Braun : Only that it was not a Norse dimension. The machine is not perfect at predicting what dimensions it finds are part of the nine realms, so it opens all that it finds. Considering that, he apparently believed he would still be able to find these worlds from where he was at and complete the project. I know I may have worked for him and the Nazi’s, but I swear I never wanted any of this. I fear the day he may return with whatever arsenal of mythological artifacts he may find or worse, find a way to destroy the world as we know it and begin again.

(extraneous dialogue excluded)

